      "statement": "What tells the alerts apart, given that both have 6 senders and 6 transfers inside one event-time hour: (a) Amounts: 357000 in varied amounts for alert 1, against 15000 in six identical 2500 transfers for alert 2. (b) Onward reach: for alert 1 all contributing transfers are passed on through 3 links to one resting account; for alert 2 half are passed on, through 1 link. (c) Devices: for alert 1, one device (D-568) sent every onward hop from three different route accounts; for alert 2 there is no device sharing on the route. (d) Timing: alert 1's onward hops follow each other 140000 to 195000 ms apart. None of the intermediate or resting route accounts (A-5092, A-2897, A-4989, A-1415) has a fan-in alert of its own.",
